@meta
id: 22-10
title: Back to the same lines
chapter: 22
type: lesson
skills: gv-reselect, visual-line
par: 64
minutes: 5
vscode: the selection survives Replace All, so you never needed this
open: order.provider.ts

@brief
An Ex command run from a selection drops the selection when it
finishes. `:s` on three lines leaves you in normal mode on the last of
them, and if those same three lines now need a second thing done to
them you are back to selecting.

`gv` reselects the last visual region, in the same mode it was made.
Same lines, same columns, ready for the next operator.

Three lines were moved into the new `if` block in `cancel` from a
helper. In the helper the variable was `order`; here it is
`cancelled`. And they came in one level too shallow. Fix both:
`order.` becomes `cancelled.` on those three lines, and the three lines
move in one level.

@keys
| `gv` | reselect the last visual selection |
| `:'<,'>s/old/new/g` | substitute on the selection |
| `>` | shift the selection right one level |

@hints
Select the three lines with `V2j` from the first `await`, do the
substitute from the `:'<,'>` range. Now you are in normal mode with
nothing selected.
--
`gv` brings the three lines back, highlighted. `>` shifts them.
--
`/await this.payment` `Enter`, `V2j`, `:s/order\./cancelled\./g`
`Enter`, then `gv` and `>`.

@solution
    /await this.payment<Enter> V 2 j :s/order\./cancelled\./g<Enter> g v > :wq<Enter>

Fifty-five keystrokes, twenty-five of them the substitute. The two keys that
matter are `gv`. Without them, `>` after the `:s` would have shifted
one line — the one the cursor happened to end on — and `.` would have
repeated the substitute, not the shift.

`gv` is also how you check what an operator just did: `d` something,
`u` to put it back, `gv` to see the region you had, adjust, and go
again. And it works after `Esc`: drop a selection to look at something
else, `gv` picks it up exactly where it was.

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
  ) {}

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const cancelled = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!cancelled) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    const days = (Date.now() - cancelled.placedAt.getTime()) / 86_400_000;

    if (days <= 30) {
    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);
    await this.emailService.send(order.customerId, 'refund-issued');
    await this.orderRepository.update({ where: { id: order.id }, values: { refunded: true } });
    }

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
  ) {}

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const cancelled = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!cancelled) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    const days = (Date.now() - cancelled.placedAt.getTime()) / 86_400_000;

    if (days <= 30) {
      await this.paymentService.refund(cancelled.id);
      await this.emailService.send(cancelled.customerId, 'refund-issued');
      await this.orderRepository.update({ where: { id: cancelled.id }, values: { refunded: true } });
    }

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}
